<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Introducing Panama to the World – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Scenario:</b> International Communication</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Theme:</b> Introducing Panama to the World</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Compose opinion essays on broad topics. Interactive: Provide feedback on narrative writing.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can compose an opinion essay on Panama's role in international relations (e.g., "The Panama Canal strengthens global trade by reducing travel time between continents, making Panama a strategic trade partner and economic hub for international companies. Additionally, Panama's diplomatic efforts, such as hosting international summits, demonstrate its commitment to fostering cooperation and dialogue among nations.")
Can edit narrative texts for clarity and style, providing feedback to peers related to Panama's global or national significance (e.g., "I think you can improve your story by adding more details about Panama's role in international trade.")
Can offer feedback on essays about Panama's relevance and impact, focusing on structure and argument strength (e.g., "Your essay needs clearer topic sentences to guide the reader through your points.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b><br>Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> Students watch a short video (1-2 minutes) showing images of Panama (Canal, biodiversity, modern city, indigenous groups) with background music. After the video, the teacher asks students to quickly jot down 3-5 keywords or phrases that come to mind about Panama's global relevance or impact. Students then share their keywords with a partner, activating vocabulary like "trade," "global," "biodiversity," "hub," "strategic."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher projects a sentence: "Panama is recognized globally for its strategic position in international trade." The teacher highlights "is recognized" (passive voice) and "strategic" (adjective). The teacher then models the pronunciation of "trade" /treɪd/ and "global" /ˈɡloʊ.bəl/, emphasizing the /t/ and /g/ sounds. The teacher also models stressing a modal verb in a sentence: "Students <b>MUST</b> be proficient in English to engage internationally," ensuring students hear the emphasis on "MUST." The teacher explains that writing an opinion essay requires stating a clear opinion and supporting it with evidence.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Who performs the action in 'Panama is recognized globally'? Is it Panama, or other people?" (Expected answer: "Other people.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is a 'strategic' position? Does it mean it's unimportant or very important for a goal?" (Expected answer: "Very important for a goal.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b><br>Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "International Communication"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short (approx. 150-200 words) model opinion essay excerpt titled "Panama's Indispensable Role in Global Commerce." The essay uses passive voice, modals of necessity, and relative clauses, along with target vocabulary (e.g., "trade," "hub," "multinational companies," "financial services," "impact," "ensure"). The register is formal and academic, suitable for international communication.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Produces written texts clearly and coherently, expressing opinions on general and abstract topics, justifying them with arguments and examples.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Question:</b> "What is the main argument of this essay about Panama's role?" (Students identify the overall opinion presented.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students read 3-4 statements about the essay's content and mark them as True or False. For example: "The essay states that Panama's economy is mainly based on agriculture." (False) "Panama is considered a financial hub that attracts multinational companies." (True)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">8-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b><br>Accuracy focus on Writing</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice using passive voice, modals of necessity (must, should), and relative clauses (that, which, where) in written sentences, integrating vocabulary such as "trade," "relevance," "impact," "financial services," "companies," "hub," "strategic," "ensure," "recognize."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Sentence Completion):</b> Students receive a worksheet with sentences about Panama's global role. They complete the sentences using the correct passive voice form of a given verb, a modal of necessity, or a relative pronoun.
                        <br><i>Examples:</i>
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Panama ______ (recognize) for its diverse biodiversity." (is recognized)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Ecotourists ______ (must/should) respect the natural protected areas." (must respect)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"The Panama Canal is a waterway ______ (connect) two major oceans." (that connects)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Sentence Expansion/Combination):</b> Students are given pairs of simple sentences related to Panama. They must combine these into one complex sentence using a relative clause or rewrite them using the passive voice, incorporating appropriate vocabulary.
                        <br><i>Examples:</i>
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Panama City offers financial services. Many multinational companies are based there." -> "Panama City offers financial services, where many multinational companies are based."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"People know Panama for its trade influence." -> "Panama is known for its trade influence."</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Peer Check:</b> In pairs, students exchange their completed worksheets from activity 2. They review each other's sentences for grammatical accuracy (passive voice, modals, relative clauses) and appropriate vocabulary use. They provide brief written feedback, like, "Good use of 'which' here," or "Check passive voice form in sentence 3."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">12-15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b><br>Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "International Communication"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Individual opinion essay composition.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Description:</b> Students will write a short (150-200 words) opinion essay responding to the prompt: "In what ways does Panama’s geographical position and cultural diversity contribute to its global relevance and impact?" They must support their opinion with at least two distinct arguments, using evidence (previously discussed or general knowledge). The essay must incorporate at least two instances of passive voice, two modals of necessity, and two relative clauses, along with a minimum of five vocabulary words from the list (e.g., "trade," "biodiversity," "hub," "strategic," "financial services," "impact," "multinational").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Actions:</b> The teacher circulates, offering guidance on essay structure (introduction of opinion, body paragraphs with arguments and examples, conclusion), vocabulary choices, and grammatical accuracy. The teacher reminds students to focus on clear topic sentences to guide the reader through their points, as per the learning outcome.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">15-18 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b><br>Formative assessment strategy</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Peer feedback using a simplified checklist/rubric.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students exchange their opinion essays with a new partner. Each student uses a provided checklist to review their peer's essay, focusing on:</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of the main opinion.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Strength and support of arguments.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of passive voice, modals, and relative clauses.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate vocabulary.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Overall coherence and structure (e.g., "Your essay needs clearer topic sentences to guide the reader through your points.").</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Peers provide specific, constructive written feedback on the essay draft. The teacher monitors and facilitates the feedback process, ensuring feedback is respectful and helpful (e.g., "I think you can improve your story by adding more details about Panama's role in international trade.").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of written arguments and opinion.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target grammar (passive voice, modals, relative clauses).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Integration of target vocabulary.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Coherence and cohesion of the essay (paragraphing, topic sentences).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Constructiveness and clarity of peer feedback.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students reflect on their own writing process and the feedback received.</p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one thing I will improve in my essay based on my partner's feedback?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Which grammatical structure (passive voice, modals, relative clauses) do I feel most confident using in my writing now?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">8-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How has my ability to express opinions about Panama's global role improved through writing this essay?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What challenges did I face when trying to incorporate new grammar or vocabulary into my writing, and how can I overcome them?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this lesson? (e.g., student engagement with essay topic, effective peer feedback, good application of specific grammar points).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson? (e.g., more direct instruction on paragraph structuring, additional support for vocabulary recall during writing, reviewing common errors from essays).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> The written essays and peer feedback from this lesson will serve as a foundation for Lesson 5, where students will refine their arguments and present their perspectives on Panama's global significance in a collaborative 21st Century Skills Project, potentially requiring them to mediate information or summarize their opinions for a broader audience.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>